# better-auth declares OPTIONAL peer dependencies for every framework it
# supports (@sveltejs/kit, @tanstack/react-start, ...). npm tries to satisfy
# them, picks @sveltejs/vite-plugin-svelte@7, and that is the only thing in the
# chain demanding vite 8 — which collides with vitest 1.6's vite 5.
#
# We use none of those frameworks, and with this flag none of them install, so
# vite/vitest stay exactly where they were. Verified 2026-08-01. An `overrides`
# pin does NOT work; the conflict regenerates through the other framework peers.
#
# The flag is not purely additive, though: npm no longer pulls electron-builder's
# optional Windows signing peers, so electron-builder-squirrel-windows,
# electron-winstaller and @electron/windows-sign left the lockfile. We ship a mac
# DMG and a linux AppImage/deb and build no Windows target, so nothing breaks
# today — but adding a Windows build means adding those three explicitly.
#
# The real reason this is not optional: `npm ci --omit=dev` FAILS without it, so
# the production deploy breaks.
#
# Cost, accepted deliberately: this disables peer checking repo-wide and could
# mask a genuine conflict later.
legacy-peer-deps=true
